On Thu, Jan 13, 2011 at 12:31 AM, Ross Ogilvie <oges007@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> Is the suggestion being entertained
> si = delete word
> sa = delete sentence
> su = delete everything
> ?

More or less, with caveats.

"si" deletes a word or a magic-word construct. Magic-word constructs
for some purposes (basically interaction with other magic words)
behave as single words.

"sa" wouldn't normally delete an actual sentence, but rather a
sentence attempt. Often just a string of words that don't form
anything grammatical.

"su" doesn't always delete everything with the current PEG, but I
would be in favor of making it stronger so that it does actually
delete everything.

